    "media:imagetext": "1934\nTHE S-42 WAS DESIGNED AND BUILT FOR PAN AMERICAN. CLEANER LINES THAN\nTHE S-40,\nSHORTENED\nTHE S-40, THE S-42 SHORTENED THE TIME TO BUENOS AIRES AND ALSO WAS\nUSED TO SURVEY PAA'S PACIFIC ROUTES. IN JULY, 1937, A S-42 FLYING\nBOAT MADE THE FIRST REGULAR AIRLINE CROSSING OF THE NORTH ATLANTIC\nOCEAN STARTING FROM\nOCEAN STARTING FROM THE UNITED STATES, FLYING FIRST TO ENGLAND BY THE\nNORTHERN\nNORTHERN ROUTE, AND THEN TO PORTUGAL BY THE BERMUDA-AZORES ROUTE. THE\nd 2PEO SIT\nCLIPPER CARRIED 32 PASSENGERS IN LUXURIOUS COMPARTMENTS.",
